## ***********************************************************************
## **
## **  KB.INC.BL -- the keyboard buffer, emptied.
## **
## **      KB.CLEARKB     throw away whatever is already typed
## **
## **  Requires GPB.INC.BL, and does not #INCLUDE it for you.
## **
## **  THIS IS THE LOW MEMORY ONE. GUI.INC.BL carries a private twin,
## **  GUI.CLEARKB, because code inside a GP.BANKED region may not call another
## **  bank and survive the return. Fix one and fix the other; there are only
## **  the two, and a second #INCLUDE of this file cannot supply the twin --
## **  #IFNDEF KB.DEFS makes it produce nothing.
## **
## **  THIS IS THE BANKED FORM. Every entry point carries a .BODY suffix,
## **  because a banked routine cannot select its own bank: the public name
## **  has to be a shim in low memory, and SHIM.UTILBANK.INC.BL holds it.
## **  Put this file inside the GP.BANKED region, with that shim above it.
## **
## **  The low memory twin is KB.INC.BL. Include one or the other, never both:
## **  the #IFNDEF guard is the same name in each, so the second one read
## **  produces nothing and the labels it was wanted for are missing.
## **
## ***********************************************************************
#IFNDEF KB.DEFS
#DEFINE KB.DEFS 1

GOTO KB.MODULE.END

## KB.CLEARKB -- throw away whatever is already typed.
##
## Call it before opening a dialog, and after a keystroke that redraws. A dialog opened
## with a key still queued reads it, answers itself and closes; a held arrow repeats
## faster than a page can be drawn and scrolls on after the key is let go.

KB.CLEARKB.BODY:
    GP.DO
        GET KB.K$
        IF GP.ISEMPTY(KB.K$) THEN GP.EXITDO
    GP.LOOP
    RETURN

KB.MODULE.END:
#ENDIF
